<h2>Gourmet Pairing &amp; Side Recommendations</h2>
<p>Because the Mushroom Swiss brings rich, creamy dairy and earthiness, pairing it with textural crunch creates the ultimate dining harmony:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The Steakhouse Classic:</strong> Mushroom Swiss + <a href="/items/onion-rings">Crispy Battered Onion Rings</a> ($3.29) = $12.78; sweet Spanish onions and crunchy batter mirror high-end chophouse presentations.</li>
<li><strong>The Lunch Standard:</strong> Mushroom Swiss + <a href="/items/regular-fries">Golden French Fries</a> ($2.49) = $11.98; hot, salty potato crisps ideal for dipping into escaping mushroom sauce.</li>
<li><strong>Sweet Dessert Contrast:</strong> Round out your visit with a classic <a href="/items/hot-fudge-sundae">Hot Fudge Sundae</a> ($3.79) to refresh the palate with cold vanilla cream.</li>
</ul>
